{#
/**
 * @file
 * The song page (INT8-019) — FR-12, FR-14, FR-15, FR-17.
 *
 * REVIEW ROUND 2 (2026-07-26): this template originally replaced core's
 * node.html.twig outright, which silently dropped the <article> wrapper,
 * `attributes` (the node--type-song / node--view-mode-full classes,
 * contextual-links attributes) and the title_prefix/title_suffix hooks other
 * modules attach to — a real accessibility/SEO and module-compatibility
 * regression, caught in review rather than by a test (nothing in this
 * project's suite asserts the node's own wrapper element). Rebuilt to keep
 * that structure, mirroring core/starterkit's own node.html.twig, with only
 * the CONTENT arrangement inside customised.
 *
 * The page's one <h1> is supplied site-wide by INT8-028's page-header hero
 * block, not by this template — so unlike core's own node.html.twig (which
 * conditionally prints an <h2> title when `view_mode != 'full'`), no title
 * heading is printed here at all: this template is suffixed `--full`, so
 * that condition is always false for it anyway.
 *
 * FR-12's negative half (no type/group) and FR-14 (no releases, setlist,
 * tabs, studio) are satisfied by OMISSION: `field_song_type`,
 * `field_parent_song` and friends are hidden on the `full` view display
 * (core.entity_view_display.node.song.full.yml) and nothing below prints
 * them by name. There is no suppression logic to get wrong.
 *
 * Field ORDER is controlled here, not by the display's field weights: the
 * hi-fi's SONG PAGE composition puts the quote ABOVE the lyrics, which a
 * plain field-order render can't express without reordering every other
 * field's weight to match — the quote is the one field genuinely out of
 * document order relative to the rest.
 *
 * `content.field_x|render|trim` (not `node.field_x.isEmpty()`) is the
 * emptiness check throughout: it asks "would this actually render
 * something", which also respects field access — a field an anonymous
 * visitor cannot see is correctly treated as absent, not merely unset.
 *
 * The "coming soon" rail moved out of this template entirely (review round
 * 2) — it is now the `i8_song_sidebar` block, placed in the theme's new
 * `sidebar_second` region and composed into a real two-column layout by
 * page.html.twig, not hardcoded here. It held no field content and needed
 * no per-node data, so a block was strictly the right shape for it — this
 * template only ever needed to render the node's own fields.
 */
#}
{%
  set classes = [
    'node',
    'node--type-' ~ node.bundle|clean_class,
    node.isPromoted() ? 'node--promoted',
    node.isSticky() ? 'node--sticky',
    not node.isPublished() ? 'node--unpublished',
    'node--view-mode-' ~ view_mode|clean_class,
  ]
%}
{% set has_quote = content.field_quotes|render|trim %}
{% set has_lyrics = content.field_lyrics|render|trim %}
{% set has_notes = content.field_notes|render|trim %}
{% set has_video = content.field_video|render|trim %}

<article{{ attributes.addClass(classes) }}>
  {{ title_prefix }}
  {{ title_suffix }}

  <div{{ content_attributes.addClass('song-detail') }}>
    {% if has_quote %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:quote-block' %}
        {% block quote %}{{ content.field_quotes }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
    {% endif %}

    {% if has_lyrics %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:section-label' %}
        {% block label %}{{ 'Lyrics'|t }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
      <div class="song-detail__lyrics">{{ content.field_lyrics }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if has_notes %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:section-label' %}
        {% block label %}{{ 'Notes'|t }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
      <div class="song-detail__notes">{{ content.field_notes }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    {% if has_video %}
      {% embed 'interstate_85:section-label' %}
        {% block label %}{{ 'Video'|t }}{% endblock %}
      {% endembed %}
      <div class="song-detail__video">{{ content.field_video }}</div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</article>
